WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.160
it.

3
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.480
Just follow along step by step. For this prep, you'll need a few items,

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.040
all available over the counter, no prescription needed.

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:18.000
You'll need one 238-gram bottle of MiraLAX powder, two to four Dulcolax laxative tablets

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:18.000
,

7
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.960
and 64 ounces of a clear sports drink like Gatorade, Propel, or Crystal Light.

8
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.680
That's usually two 32-ounce bottles. If you have diabetes, use sugar-free Gatorade

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.160
G2.

10
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.400
Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not the stool softener.

11
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.200
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

12
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.920
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

13
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.560
The day before your colonoscopy, you'll start by mixing the solution.

14
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:49.440
Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64 ounces of the

15
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.320
sports drink,

16
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.840
stir, or shake until the powder is completely dissolved.

17
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.200
You can chill it in the refrigerator if you'd like. Keeping it cold makes it

18
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:57.840
easier to drink.

19
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.200
Now for Part 1, the evening before your procedure.

20
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.280
At 5:00 PM, take your Dulcolax tablets with a glass of water.

21
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.640
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four. Follow

22
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:08.800
their

23
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.200
guidance on the specific amount. At 6:00 PM, you'll start drinking the first half

24
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.240
of the solution.

25
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.030
That's 32 ounces. Drink an 8 ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half is

26
00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:19.440
gone.

27
00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:25.430
Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish. For Part 2, six hours before your

28
00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.480
colonoscopy,

29
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.680
you'll drink the second half, which is another 32 ounces.

30
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.160
Drink this at the same pace, an 8 ounce glass every 15 minutes.

31
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.460
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your

32
00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:38.960
procedure.

33
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.160
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

34
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.280
directed,

35
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.000
even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough,

36
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.610
but finishing the entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during your

37
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:54.480
procedure.

38
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.760
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

39
00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.480
of us wants that.

40
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.960
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

41
00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.360
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

42
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.600
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

43
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.440
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

44
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:24.000
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

45
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:24.480
hydrated.

46
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.000
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

47
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.880
to help.
